From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anxelok <anxelok@localhost>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 17:21:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add caller-participates scheduling for the region tick joins

The parallel tick dispatches work as a nested fork-join: the server thread
fans the worlds onto the region pool, then each world-tick thread fans its
own chunk and entity buckets onto the same pool and waits at join(). A thread
waiting at that hand-off holds a pool thread while doing nothing, so the
dispatching threads sat idle at the barrier while only part of the pool ran
buckets.

Change the wait: instead of parking, a dispatching thread pulls ready buckets
off a shared cursor and runs them itself, and only waits for buckets still in
flight on other threads. The idle owner threads become extra workers, so more
of the pool is busy during the tick. Each bucket still runs once under its own
region ownership and lease, writes are still staged and applied per world in
the same serial order, and the chunk to block-events to entity phase order is
unchanged - only the scheduling of the compute changes.

On by default; set -Dloom.scheduler.callerParticipates=false to restore the
previous parked-join behaviour.

